WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.083
(gentle piano music)

00:00:07.409 --> 00:00:08.832
- When I have the Henna crown on,

00:00:08.832 --> 00:00:12.832
it's as if people don't see the sickness

00:00:12.832 --> 00:00:16.129
as much as they do when
your head is just bald.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:18.395
They just look and they see this

00:00:18.395 --> 00:00:21.552
beautiful artwork, and it's empowering.

00:00:21.552 --> 00:00:25.280
It's nice to feel almost normal again.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.741
- My name is Sarah Walters, and I'm

00:00:26.741 --> 00:00:28.822
a professional Henna artist.

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:32.304
The term, Henna Crown is
being used to describe

00:00:32.304 --> 00:00:35.559
intricate Henna designs
that are applied to

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:39.344
the scalp following hair loss, um, typically,

00:00:39.344 --> 00:00:42.086
so usually people will
refer to Henna crowns

00:00:42.086 --> 00:00:43.289
as being applied to people

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:45.942
who've gone through chemo therapy.

00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:49.419
I initially began doing
Henna crowns when my mom

00:00:49.419 --> 00:00:51.638
asked me to do one for her friend,

00:00:51.638 --> 00:00:54.342
who had recently lost her
hair during chemo therapy,

00:00:54.342 --> 00:00:57.845
so I agreed to do it and it
was a wonderful experience.

00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:00.110
From that point on, I knew that I wanted

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.235
to continue to offer crowns for people.

00:01:03.235 --> 00:01:05.635
- My name's Vicki Sumner, and I

00:01:05.635 --> 00:01:08.452
have stage four breast cancer.

00:01:08.452 --> 00:01:11.285
Once cancer becomes stage four and

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.995
it travels to other
organs, it then becomes

00:01:14.995 --> 00:01:18.094
a terminal diagnosis
and so everything we do,

00:01:18.094 --> 00:01:21.427
from here, is just trying to stay alive.

00:01:25.368 --> 00:01:28.368
- I'll probably start, you know, at the front,

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.950
maybe on this side or this side.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.705
- I originally looked for a Henna crown

00:01:34.705 --> 00:01:38.727
because I wanted to share
a message on my head.

00:01:38.727 --> 00:01:41.906
The message on the back
says, Stage IV needs more.

00:01:41.906 --> 00:01:44.507
Stage four breast cancer
needs more attention,

00:01:44.507 --> 00:01:47.227
for years it's been sort
of swept under the rug,

00:01:47.227 --> 00:01:50.776
nobody wanted to talk about it
because it's terminal cancer.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.781
When I go in to get my Henna crown,

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:55.478
it is like a spa-like experience.

00:01:55.478 --> 00:02:00.196
Sarah scents it with lavender
and it's calming and soothing

00:02:00.196 --> 00:02:02.757
and sometimes I nod off a little bit.

00:02:02.757 --> 00:02:05.638
It takes about an hour, hour and a half,

00:02:05.638 --> 00:02:08.736
and it's just relaxing and you wake up

00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:10.896
and see the beautiful artwork that

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:14.229
she's come up with when you're finished.

00:02:16.379 --> 00:02:18.403
My daughter loves it when I come home

00:02:18.403 --> 00:02:20.184
and I have the Henna, she's like,

00:02:20.184 --> 00:02:22.101
“Oh, you got it again!"

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:27.031
- I think that everyone is
beautiful in their own way,

00:02:27.031 --> 00:02:30.364
and I can see the beauty in these people

00:02:31.635 --> 00:02:33.395
that come to me, wanting a crown,

00:02:33.395 --> 00:02:35.347
because they're displaying a lot of

00:02:35.347 --> 00:02:38.585
strength and resilience and fight.

00:02:38.585 --> 00:02:40.441
At the same time, they're feeling

00:02:40.441 --> 00:02:44.243
maybe a lack of confidence or, you know, discomfort

00:02:44.243 --> 00:02:46.640
about the loss of their
hair and other things

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.403
that they're going through and

00:02:48.403 --> 00:02:50.085
when the crown that I do for them,

00:02:50.085 --> 00:02:52.852
gives them that boost of confidence,

00:02:52.852 --> 00:02:54.910
it's just a really awesome feeling

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.678
because it does make them
feel a little more beautiful,

00:02:57.678 --> 00:02:59.214
I think in some cases.

00:02:59.214 --> 00:03:00.092
- So pretty.

00:03:00.092 --> 00:03:00.925
- Yay!

00:03:00.925 --> 00:03:02.925
I'm so glad you like it.

00:03:04.318 --> 00:03:06.956
- I always believe that we should try to

00:03:06.956 --> 00:03:09.220
make other people smile during the day

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.740
and that we should always do something

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.641
kind for the people around us.

00:03:13.641 --> 00:03:16.739
Sarah's one of those people;
Sarah's one of those people

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:18.558
trying to make a small difference

00:03:18.558 --> 00:03:20.777
to the people around her, by offering

00:03:20.777 --> 00:03:24.637
the Henna crowns to people
suffering from cancer,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.300
just makes the world a better place.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.883
(lively music)

